https://leetcode.com/problems/search-in-rotated-sorted-array/description/


class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {
         int low = 0;
        int high = nums.length - 1;
        // Continue while there is still a valid search range
        while (low <= high) {
            int mid = (low + high) / 2;
            // If target found, return index
            if (nums[mid] == target)
                return mid;
            // If left part is sorted
            if (nums[low] <= nums[mid]) {
                // If target lies within sorted left part
                if (nums[low] <= target && target < nums[mid]) 
                    high = mid - 1;
                // Else, search in right half
                else 
                    low = mid + 1;
            }
            // Else, right part is sorted
            else {
                // If target lies within sorted right part
                if (nums[mid] < target && target <= nums[high]) 
                    low = mid + 1;
                // Else, search in left half
                else 
                    high = mid - 1;
            }
        }
        return -1;
    }
}


The intuition is: rotation breaks global sortedness but preserves 
local sortedness in one half at every split. By checking which half is sorted, you can decide where to continue searching.
